# Expectation record for 03_initializers/009_static_vs_automatic.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 009_static_vs_automatic
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Storage duration deciding how often an initializer runs: three shape-matched pairs of function-scope static and automatic objects observed across three calls before and after an identical mutation, plus file-scope objects covering data, read-only and zero-initialized BSS placement
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
Every accumulated value is tiny, and that is what keeps the one arithmetic-carrying program in this
area free of signed overflow: s_counter peaks at 130, the s_arr elements at 301, 302 and 303, the
s_st members at 10 and 11, and g_static_scalar at 1005. The automatic twins are bounded lower still,
because each is re-initialized on entry and then mutated exactly once per call, so each ends every
call at the same value: a_counter at 110, the a_arr elements at 101, 102 and 103, and the a_st
members at 8 and 9. Every object this program mutates is therefore bounded by name, which is what
makes the argument checkable rather than merely reassuring. INT_MAX is at least 2147483647 on every
conforming target, so no sum here can approach it. The loop counters are bounded by the literals 3,
4 and 3, and the round counter by 3, and per_call is invoked a fixed three times with literal round
numbers. There is no shift, no division, no remainder and no cast anywhere in the program.
No object is modified twice between two sequence points. Each compound assignment is its own full
expression -- never embedded in a call argument -- and every printf argument is a plain read of an
object no argument of the same call modifies, so the unspecified order in which a function call's
arguments are evaluated cannot be observed even though several arguments are read per call.
NO UNINITIALIZED STORAGE IS READ. Every function-scope and file-scope object with an initializer is
fully initialized by it, and g_static_bss, which has no initializer, has STATIC storage duration, so
C11 6.7.9p10 defines its elements as zero rather than indeterminate -- a definite value, and itself
one of the properties under test. The three function-scope statics are initialized once before the
program begins rather than on each entry, which is exactly the distinction under test, and the three
automatic objects are initialized on every entry to the block, so each is readable from its first
read onward in every round.
Every subscript stays strictly inside its array bound, and each bound is a literal equal to the
declared extent: s_arr and a_arr are int[3] read at 0 through 2, g_static_arr is int[4] read at 0
through 3, and g_static_const and g_static_bss are int[3] read at 0 through 2. With every subscript
in bounds, the pointer arithmetic the language performs for it stays inside its object: no
one-past-the-end pointer is dereferenced, no address of an object is taken, and no pointer value is
printed, compared or converted to an integer. The only other pointers in the program are the
format-string literals decaying at each printf call.
There is no aliasing violation: every value is read and written through an lvalue of its own declared
type, which is int in every case, reached by member selection and subscripting. g_static_const is
declared const and is only ever READ -- never written, and never reached through a non-const lvalue
-- so no attempt to modify an object defined with a const-qualified type occurs. g_static_scalar is
not const and is mutated once after the call loop, which is what demonstrates that a data-section
object is writable. No object representation is inspected, no union appears, and no struct is copied
or printed whole, so no padding byte is ever observed and nothing depends on the relative addresses
of unrelated objects.
Each printf conversion specifier is %d and each corresponding argument has type int after the default
argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by the
operating system. Every input is a literal in this file: nothing is read from the environment, the
clock, the file system or the network, and iteration and call order are fixed by literal bounds, so
every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md, "9 bundled freestanding headers"), so naming one would fail on the
bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the
test rather than by a compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two,
area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12. This record declares no
warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror in the single native compile-only invocation the suite's warning gate makes, and it builds
and runs clean under the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both
gates are reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag
discipline is untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing: all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears
because the program passes the suite's full default warning gate unmodified.
THE STATIC/AUTOMATIC PAIRING IS THE WHOLE SUBJECT, so what each half must print is stated exactly.
per_call() is invoked three times over three pairs matched by shape and by initializer --
s_counter/a_counter, s_arr/a_arr, s_st/a_st -- printing all six before mutating them, applying the
SAME mutation to both halves of every pair, then printing again. Because nothing but storage
duration differs between the halves, any difference in the printed sequence is attributable to
storage duration alone. A static-duration initializer is materialized ONCE, before the program
begins; an automatic-duration initializer is materialized on EVERY entry to its block by code the
backend emits. The static halves therefore ADVANCE across rounds: s_counter reads 100, 110, 120 on
entry and 110, 120, 130 after; s_arr reads 1,2,3 then 101,102,103 then 201,202,203 on entry; s_st
reads { 7,8 } then { 8,9 } then { 9,10 } on entry and { 10,11 } after the last round. The automatic
halves are re-initialized on every entry, so their pre-mutation values are IDENTICAL every round:
a_counter is always 100, a_arr always 1,2,3, a_st always { 7,8 }, and after the mutation always
110, 101/102/103 and { 8,9 }. Round 1 is where the halves legitimately coincide, which is itself the
evidence that both were initialized correctly; rounds 2 and 3 carry the diagnostic weight. A
compiler that re-ran a function-scope static initializer on every call would print s_counter=100
three times; one that failed to re-initialize an automatic object would print a_counter=110 on entry
to round 2. Either is visible on a single line.
BOTH MEMBERS OF EVERY PAIR ARE OBSERVED. The post-mutation line prints s_st.p, s_st.q, a_st.p and
a_st.q, matching the pre-mutation line member for member. Printing only .p would leave the two .q
mutations unobserved, and a backend that dropped the increment of a struct's second member, or
mutated the wrong member, would then produce byte-identical output and escape every oracle. With
.q observed, s_st.q must advance 8, 9, 10 on entry and 9, 10, 11 after, while a_st.q reads 8 on
entry and 9 after in every round. The peaks the last round records are therefore fixed and checkable
individually: the block-scope static counter ends at 130, the static array at 301, 302 and 303, the
static struct at 10 in its first member and 11 in its second, and the file-scope scalar at 1005.
FILE SCOPE COVERS SECTION PLACEMENT, AND ONLY ITS OBSERVABLE CONSEQUENCES. An initialized scalar,
array and struct reach .data, a const array typically .rodata, and an array with no initializer at
all has static storage duration and is guaranteed zero from BSS rather than from any emitted store.
g_static_scalar is mutated after the call loop and re-read, showing that a .data object is writable,
while g_static_const is only ever read. No address is printed, so which SECTION the compiler chooses
is deliberately left free: the program asserts the observable CONSEQUENCES of placement -- that an
initialized object reads back its initializer, that a const array reads back its initializer, that an
uninitialized static array reads back zero, and that a non-const initialized object is writable --
and never the section name, so a compiler that places g_static_const in a writable section, or that
emits explicit zero bytes for g_static_bss rather than reserving BSS, is not thereby divergent.
NO OPERAND IS QUALIFIED VOLATILE ANYWHERE, BY DESIGN rather than by omission. A function-scope static
is a prime inlining and constant-propagation target, so identical output at -O0, -O1 and -O2 is a
genuine semantic-preservation check that forcing every access back to memory would SUPPRESS rather
than prove. The static/automatic pairing is itself this program's two-variant structure, and this is
the one program in the area whose optimization sweep tests the optimizer directly rather than the
initializer-emission path, which is why the sweep covers all three levels.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Only int and %d are used, so the MEASURED i686 differences -- a four-byte long
and pointer against eight bytes on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462) -- cannot be observed. No sizeof or
_Alignof result is printed and no floating value reaches a format string.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS AND PADDING. The only character data is the format-string literals, whose
bytes printf copies through unchanged; no plain-char value is read as a number, so the MEASURED
plain-char signedness split -- signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- is
irrelevant. No struct representation is printed, so padding does not matter.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. No character's numeric CODE is computed or printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves
nothing here to the implementation; the label bytes of each line are copied through printf from the
same source on both sides of every comparison.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 44 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without
any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. Every element and member
is read back individually and every in-function line carries its round number, so a single wrong
slot localizes to one initializer form in one invocation rather than to the program as a whole.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
g_static_scalar=1000
g_static_arr[0]=11
g_static_arr[1]=12
g_static_arr[2]=13
g_static_arr[3]=14
g_static_st.p=21
